  "worked_solution": "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,-5,$ and $4.$",
